      "text": "Albion, Iowa, was founded in 1852, marking the beginning of a small Midwestern community that would grow into a charming town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albion%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was first called La Fayette until it was renamed Albion in 1858, reflecting a shift in local identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albion%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Located on Section 6, Town 84, Range 18, Albion lies about seven miles northwest of Marshalltown, placing it in a rural setting.",
